<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gbadebo I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gbadebo I was the Alake of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abeokuta">Abeokuta</a>, paramount ruler of the Egba in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, from 1898 until his death in 1920. His reign coincided with the reformed Egba United Government, which ran its own treasury, courts and roads under British influence, and in 1904 he visited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and met Edward VII. After disturbances in 1914 Egba independence ended and Abeokuta was absorbed into Nigeria.</p></div>
